1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:02,004
Which expression is equivalent?

2
00:00:02,397 --> 00:00:06,770
Equivalent expressions is one of the
three skills in the SAT's Advanced Math

3
00:00:06,790 --> 00:00:10,627
domain, which is about thirty-five
percent of the math section.

4
00:00:10,647 --> 00:00:12,859
The algebra usually isn't the hard part.

5
00:00:12,879 --> 00:00:17,288
Points get lost on one small slip, and
the wrong answers are built from those

6
00:00:17,308 --> 00:00:18,145
slips.

7
00:00:18,165 --> 00:00:22,181
Here's the plan: six tools,
seven practice questions,

8
00:00:22,201 --> 00:00:26,895
the four traps behind most mistakes,
and a check you can run on any of these

9
00:00:26,915 --> 00:00:27,888
questions.

10
00:00:27,908 --> 00:00:32,530
First, equivalent means equal for every
value of x where both are defined,

11
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:33,816
not just one.

12
00:00:33,836 --> 00:00:36,651
That idea is behind every shortcut later.

13
00:00:36,671 --> 00:00:40,114
Tool one: distribute,
then combine like terms,

14
00:00:40,134 --> 00:00:42,921
meaning the same variable
raised to the same power.

15
00:00:42,954 --> 00:00:46,577
The big danger is a minus
sign in front of parentheses.

16
00:00:46,597 --> 00:00:50,006
It multiplies every term
inside, not just the first.

17
00:00:50,026 --> 00:00:54,219
Five x plus two, minus the
quantity three x minus six,

18
00:00:54,239 --> 00:00:56,934
becomes five x plus two, minus three x,

19
00:00:56,954 --> 00:00:57,827
plus six.

20
00:00:57,847 --> 00:00:59,883
That's two x plus eight.

21
00:00:59,915 --> 00:01:03,308
Tool two: factoring, which
is distributing in reverse.

22
00:01:03,736 --> 00:01:06,451
Always start with the
greatest common factor.

23
00:01:06,629 --> 00:01:10,751
Six x squared plus nine x
has three x in both terms,

24
00:01:10,771 --> 00:01:15,160
so it's three x times the
quantity two x plus three.

25
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:17,323
Next, the difference of squares.

26
00:01:17,430 --> 00:01:20,731
a squared minus b
squared equals a minus b,

27
00:01:20,751 --> 00:01:22,767
times a plus b.

28
00:01:22,787 --> 00:01:26,231
So x squared minus
forty-nine is x minus seven,

29
00:01:26,251 --> 00:01:28,001
times x plus seven.

30
00:01:28,287 --> 00:01:32,410
And four x squared minus
nine is two x minus three,

31
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:34,501
times two x plus three.

32
00:01:34,535 --> 00:01:38,393
For a trinomial like x squared
minus two x minus twenty-four,

33
00:01:38,428 --> 00:01:43,373
find two numbers that multiply to negative
twenty-four and add to negative two.

34
00:01:43,393 --> 00:01:47,658
That's negative six and four,
so it factors into x minus six,

35
00:01:47,678 --> 00:01:49,333
times x plus four.

36
00:01:49,353 --> 00:01:51,475
When the leading coefficient isn't one,

37
00:01:51,495 --> 00:01:53,869
guess and check by multiplying back.

38
00:01:53,889 --> 00:01:58,297
Two x squared plus seven x
plus three is two x plus one,

39
00:01:58,317 --> 00:02:00,440
times x plus three.

40
00:02:00,460 --> 00:02:02,684
And with four terms, try grouping.

41
00:02:02,704 --> 00:02:07,826
Take x cubed plus two x squared
minus nine x minus eighteen.

42
00:02:07,846 --> 00:02:10,755
Pull x squared out of the first two terms,

43
00:02:10,775 --> 00:02:13,576
and negative nine out of the last two.

44
00:02:13,596 --> 00:02:15,969
Both groups leave x plus two.

45
00:02:15,989 --> 00:02:20,326
So it's x plus two, times
x squared minus nine,

46
00:02:20,346 --> 00:02:22,898
which factors again into x minus three,

47
00:02:22,918 --> 00:02:25,182
times x plus three.

48
00:02:25,202 --> 00:02:27,396
Tool three: exponent rules.

49
00:02:27,416 --> 00:02:30,825
Multiplying powers of the
same base, add the exponents.

50
00:02:30,845 --> 00:02:32,467
Dividing, subtract them.

51
00:02:32,487 --> 00:02:34,932
A power of a power, multiply them.

52
00:02:34,952 --> 00:02:39,344
And an exponent outside parentheses
applies to every factor inside.

53
00:02:39,374 --> 00:02:41,604
A negative exponent means reciprocal:

54
00:02:41,624 --> 00:02:44,838
x to the negative two
is one over x squared.

55
00:02:44,945 --> 00:02:46,639
A fractional exponent means a root.

56
00:02:46,659 --> 00:02:50,925
The bottom number is the root,
and the top number is the power.

57
00:02:50,945 --> 00:02:54,532
So twenty-seven to the two thirds
is the cube root of twenty-seven,

58
00:02:54,552 --> 00:02:57,347
which is three, squared, which is nine.

59
00:02:57,367 --> 00:03:02,383
One rule to burn in: exponents and
roots spread over multiplication,

60
00:03:02,403 --> 00:03:04,224
never over addition.

61
00:03:04,616 --> 00:03:08,526
x plus four, squared, is
not x squared plus sixteen.

62
00:03:08,546 --> 00:03:11,597
It's x squared plus eight x plus sixteen.

63
00:03:11,617 --> 00:03:17,474
And the square root of the quantity x
squared plus sixteen is not x plus four.

64
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:21,607
Tool four: rational expressions,
which are fractions with variables.

65
00:03:21,627 --> 00:03:24,500
To add or subtract them,
get a common denominator,

66
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,892
just like with numbers.

67
00:03:25,912 --> 00:03:28,857
To simplify, factor the
top and bottom completely,

68
00:03:28,877 --> 00:03:30,948
then cancel matching factors.

69
00:03:30,995 --> 00:03:33,066
Cancel factors, not terms.

70
00:03:33,245 --> 00:03:36,617
Three x plus six, over
three, is x plus two,

71
00:03:36,637 --> 00:03:39,224
because three is a
factor of the whole top.

72
00:03:39,244 --> 00:03:43,189
But x plus six, over
six, is not x plus one.

73
00:03:43,209 --> 00:03:45,995
That six is only a term,
so you can't cancel it.

74
00:03:46,025 --> 00:03:48,989
Tool five: finding a missing constant.

75
00:03:49,096 --> 00:03:53,432
If two expressions are equivalent, the
coefficients of like terms have to match.

76
00:03:53,452 --> 00:03:58,504
If three times the quantity two x minus
k equals six x minus twenty-one for all

77
00:03:58,524 --> 00:04:02,549
x, then three k equals
twenty-one, so k is seven.

78
00:04:02,569 --> 00:04:05,676
Tool six is your safety
net: the plug-in check.

79
00:04:05,747 --> 00:04:10,262
Pick a number like two or three, and
evaluate the original and each choice.

80
00:04:10,282 --> 00:04:14,298
Avoid zero and one, because different
expressions can agree there.

81
00:04:14,318 --> 00:04:18,345
x squared and x cubed are
both one when x is one.

82
00:04:18,365 --> 00:04:20,972
If two choices match, try a second number.

83
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:24,401
Or use Desmos: graph the
original and a choice.

84
00:04:24,651 --> 00:04:27,095
If the graphs land exactly
on top of each other,

85
00:04:27,115 --> 00:04:28,115
they're equivalent.

86
00:04:28,185 --> 00:04:31,005
On the test, these show up in a few forms.

87
00:04:31,435 --> 00:04:33,951
Which expression is
equivalent to this one.

88
00:04:33,971 --> 00:04:35,807
Which expression is a factor.

89
00:04:35,827 --> 00:04:39,471
For what value of a constant
are two expressions equivalent.

90
00:04:39,542 --> 00:04:42,665
And rewrites with exponents or radicals,

91
00:04:42,685 --> 00:04:46,185
usually with a condition
like x is greater than zero.

92
00:04:46,238 --> 00:04:47,238
Question one.

93
00:04:47,309 --> 00:04:52,075
Which expression is equivalent to the
quantity four x squared minus three x plus

94
00:04:52,095 --> 00:04:57,344
five, minus the quantity two x
squared minus seven x minus one?

95
00:04:57,376 --> 00:04:58,591
Pause and try it.

96
00:05:01,787 --> 00:05:05,194
Distribute the minus sign to all
three terms in the second group:

97
00:05:05,214 --> 00:05:08,965
minus two x squared,
plus seven x, plus one.

98
00:05:09,214 --> 00:05:10,394
Now combine.

99
00:05:10,679 --> 00:05:14,124
Four x squared minus two x
squared is two x squared.

100
00:05:14,144 --> 00:05:17,159
Negative three x plus seven x is four x.

101
00:05:17,179 --> 00:05:19,409
Five plus one is six.

102
00:05:19,429 --> 00:05:21,108
The answer is C.

103
00:05:21,128 --> 00:05:24,179
A only changes the sign of the first term.

104
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:27,393
B flips the x term but
misses the last one.

105
00:05:27,413 --> 00:05:31,071
And D adds the polynomials
instead of subtracting.

106
00:05:31,091 --> 00:05:32,949
Each trap is one sign.

107
00:05:32,988 --> 00:05:34,166
Question two.

108
00:05:34,274 --> 00:05:38,952
Which expression is equivalent
to two x cubed minus fifty x?

109
00:05:38,986 --> 00:05:40,200
Pause and try it.

110
00:05:43,396 --> 00:05:45,626
Greatest common factor first.

111
00:05:45,646 --> 00:05:48,305
Both terms have two x, so pull it out:

112
00:05:48,325 --> 00:05:52,396
two x times the quantity x
squared minus twenty-five.

113
00:05:52,538 --> 00:05:56,232
And x squared minus twenty-five
is a difference of squares:

114
00:05:56,252 --> 00:05:59,233
x minus five, times x plus five.

115
00:05:59,253 --> 00:06:00,825
The answer is B.

116
00:06:00,859 --> 00:06:05,196
A squares x minus five, which creates a
middle term the original doesn't have.

117
00:06:05,216 --> 00:06:07,767
C uses twenty-five instead
of its square root.

118
00:06:07,787 --> 00:06:10,598
And D drops the x from the common factor.

119
00:06:10,618 --> 00:06:11,527
Question three.

120
00:06:11,547 --> 00:06:16,277
Which expression is equivalent to
the quantity sixteen x to the eighth,

121
00:06:16,297 --> 00:06:20,559
raised to the three fourths power,
where x is greater than zero?

122
00:06:20,579 --> 00:06:21,793
Pause and try it.

123
00:06:24,989 --> 00:06:27,345
The exponent applies to both factors.

124
00:06:27,524 --> 00:06:30,719
For sixteen, three fourths
means take the fourth root,

125
00:06:30,739 --> 00:06:31,846
then cube it.

126
00:06:32,025 --> 00:06:36,452
The fourth root of sixteen is
two, and two cubed is eight.

127
00:06:36,632 --> 00:06:40,433
For x to the eighth, a power
of a power means multiply:

128
00:06:40,453 --> 00:06:43,005
eight times three fourths is six.

129
00:06:43,025 --> 00:06:44,612
So it's eight x to the sixth.

130
00:06:44,632 --> 00:06:46,453
The answer is D.

131
00:06:46,535 --> 00:06:48,800
A multiplies sixteen by three fourths,

132
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:50,729
which isn't what an exponent does.

133
00:06:50,749 --> 00:06:53,621
B takes the fourth root
but forgets to cube.

134
00:06:53,641 --> 00:06:56,891
And C adds the exponents
instead of multiplying them.

135
00:06:56,921 --> 00:06:57,865
Question four.

136
00:06:57,885 --> 00:07:02,401
Which expression is equivalent to
four over the quantity x plus three,

137
00:07:02,421 --> 00:07:05,544
minus two over the quantity x minus one,

138
00:07:05,564 --> 00:07:07,447
for x greater than one?

139
00:07:07,467 --> 00:07:08,681
Pause and try it.

140
00:07:12,877 --> 00:07:15,500
The common denominator is x plus three,

141
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:17,322
times x minus one.

142
00:07:17,342 --> 00:07:19,999
Multiply the first top by x minus one,

143
00:07:20,019 --> 00:07:22,821
and the second top by x plus three.

144
00:07:22,841 --> 00:07:26,857
The numerator becomes four
times the quantity x minus one,

145
00:07:26,877 --> 00:07:30,497
minus two times the quantity x plus three.

146
00:07:30,517 --> 00:07:33,568
Distribute carefully: four x minus four,

147
00:07:33,588 --> 00:07:35,783
minus two x, minus six.

148
00:07:35,803 --> 00:07:37,710
That's two x minus ten.

149
00:07:37,730 --> 00:07:39,660
The answer is A.

150
00:07:39,894 --> 00:07:43,767
B makes the classic sign error:
minus two times three is minus six,

151
00:07:43,787 --> 00:07:45,053
not plus six.

152
00:07:45,073 --> 00:07:47,909
C multiplies each top
by its own denominator.

153
00:07:47,929 --> 00:07:51,088
And D subtracts the numerators
without rewriting them.

154
00:07:51,108 --> 00:07:55,410
Plug in two to confirm: the
original is four fifths minus two,

155
00:07:55,430 --> 00:07:58,323
negative six fifths, and only A matches.

156
00:07:58,357 --> 00:08:00,372
You've already seen the sign trap twice.

157
00:08:00,392 --> 00:08:02,837
Here are all four traps in one place.

158
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:06,408
One: distributing a negative to
only part of the parentheses.

159
00:08:06,428 --> 00:08:08,944
Two: squaring a sum term by term.

160
00:08:08,964 --> 00:08:12,265
Three: splitting a power
or a root over a plus sign.

161
00:08:12,285 --> 00:08:15,135
Four: cancelling terms instead of factors.

162
00:08:15,155 --> 00:08:16,885
Here's one built on trap four.

163
00:08:16,905 --> 00:08:20,635
Which expression is equivalent
to x squared plus five x,

164
00:08:20,655 --> 00:08:24,727
over x squared minus twenty-five,
for x greater than five?

165
00:08:24,772 --> 00:08:25,986
Pause and try it.

166
00:08:29,182 --> 00:08:31,912
The tempting move is to
cancel the x squared terms,

167
00:08:31,932 --> 00:08:33,448
which gives choice A.

168
00:08:33,468 --> 00:08:35,983
But x squared is only a term.

169
00:08:36,003 --> 00:08:37,019
Factor first.

170
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:40,768
The top is x times the
quantity x plus five.

171
00:08:40,788 --> 00:08:45,039
The bottom is x minus
five, times x plus five.

172
00:08:45,092 --> 00:08:48,520
Now x plus five is a factor
of both, so cancel it.

173
00:08:48,663 --> 00:08:52,250
That leaves x over the
quantity x minus five.

174
00:08:52,270 --> 00:08:53,805
The answer is C.

175
00:08:53,985 --> 00:08:58,306
B cancels the wrong factor,
and D cancels the x too.

176
00:08:58,342 --> 00:09:02,429
To check, plug in six: the
original is sixty-six over eleven,

177
00:09:02,449 --> 00:09:05,869
which is six, and only C gives six.

178
00:09:05,889 --> 00:09:07,032
Question six.

179
00:09:07,139 --> 00:09:12,333
If the quantity a x plus five, times
the quantity three x minus two,

180
00:09:12,353 --> 00:09:17,512
equals twelve x squared plus b
x minus ten for all values of x,

181
00:09:17,532 --> 00:09:21,148
where a and b are constants,
what is the value of b?

182
00:09:21,168 --> 00:09:22,382
Pause and try it.

183
00:09:26,578 --> 00:09:29,772
For all values of x means
the two sides are equivalent,

184
00:09:29,792 --> 00:09:31,272
so match coefficients.

185
00:09:31,292 --> 00:09:33,058
Multiply out the left side.

186
00:09:33,078 --> 00:09:36,094
The x squared term is three a x squared.

187
00:09:36,114 --> 00:09:39,915
The x terms are negative
two a x plus fifteen x.

188
00:09:39,935 --> 00:09:43,499
And the constant is negative
ten, which already matches.

189
00:09:43,519 --> 00:09:47,213
Match the x squared terms:
three a equals twelve,

190
00:09:47,233 --> 00:09:48,856
so a is four.

191
00:09:48,876 --> 00:09:54,035
Then match the x terms: b equals
negative two a plus fifteen.

192
00:09:54,055 --> 00:09:56,946
That's negative eight plus
fifteen, which is seven.

193
00:09:56,966 --> 00:10:00,160
If you entered four, you found a, not b.

194
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:03,716
If you got twenty-three, you
dropped the negative on two a.

195
00:10:03,822 --> 00:10:05,731
Last one, and the hardest.

196
00:10:05,751 --> 00:10:09,659
Which expression is equivalent to
the quantity two x minus three,

197
00:10:09,679 --> 00:10:12,872
squared, minus the quantity x plus one,

198
00:10:12,892 --> 00:10:13,714
squared?

199
00:10:13,734 --> 00:10:14,571
Pause and try it.

200
00:10:14,591 --> 00:10:16,234
Take a little longer on this one.

201
00:10:20,443 --> 00:10:22,265
One way is to expand.

202
00:10:22,336 --> 00:10:28,137
Two x minus three, squared, is four
x squared minus twelve x plus nine.

203
00:10:28,157 --> 00:10:32,923
x plus one, squared, is x
squared plus two x plus one.

204
00:10:32,943 --> 00:10:38,459
Subtract all of it, and you get three
x squared minus fourteen x plus eight.

205
00:10:38,479 --> 00:10:39,566
But that's not a choice.

206
00:10:39,586 --> 00:10:41,158
The choices are factored.

207
00:10:41,218 --> 00:10:42,377
So use the structure.

208
00:10:42,397 --> 00:10:44,305
This is a square minus a square.

209
00:10:44,325 --> 00:10:49,039
Call two x minus three
A, and x plus one B.

210
00:10:49,075 --> 00:10:52,234
A squared minus B squared is A minus B,

211
00:10:52,254 --> 00:10:54,460
times A plus B.

212
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:58,639
A minus B is two x minus three, minus x,

213
00:10:58,659 --> 00:11:01,103
minus one, which is x minus four.

214
00:11:01,123 --> 00:11:03,781
A plus B is three x minus two.

215
00:11:03,801 --> 00:11:08,246
So the answer is x minus
four, times three x minus two.

216
00:11:08,266 --> 00:11:09,281
That's D.

217
00:11:09,301 --> 00:11:12,301
Multiply it out, and it
matches the expanded form.

218
00:11:12,353 --> 00:11:13,603
Now the traps.

219
00:11:13,675 --> 00:11:15,924
A squares each term separately.

220
00:11:16,032 --> 00:11:19,333
B subtracts only the x squared term.

221
00:11:19,353 --> 00:11:21,940
C makes a sign slip inside A minus B.

222
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:25,476
Plug in two to check: the
original is one minus nine,

223
00:11:25,496 --> 00:11:26,833
negative eight.

224
00:11:26,853 --> 00:11:29,833
A gives twenty, B gives two, C gives zero,

225
00:11:29,853 --> 00:11:31,904
and only D gives negative eight.

226
00:11:31,924 --> 00:11:35,118
Or graph the original and
each choice in Desmos.

227
00:11:35,138 --> 00:11:39,245
Only D's parabola lands
exactly on top of the original.

228
00:11:39,271 --> 00:11:42,556
Here's the method for any
equivalent expressions question.

229
00:11:42,914 --> 00:11:45,751
Step one: read the choices first.

230
00:11:45,771 --> 00:11:49,500
Their form tells you the goal:
factored choices mean factor,

231
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:51,879
and expanded choices mean expand.

232
00:11:52,056 --> 00:11:55,287
Step two: look for structure,
like a common factor,

233
00:11:55,307 --> 00:11:57,879
a difference of squares,
or a perfect square.

234
00:11:57,933 --> 00:12:00,556
Step three: slow down
where the traps live.

235
00:12:00,576 --> 00:12:04,484
Every negative sign, every
exponent, every cancel.

236
00:12:04,504 --> 00:12:09,198
Step four: verify with a plug-in
number or Desmos before you click.

237
00:12:09,218 --> 00:12:13,326
And on a missing constant question,
answer the letter they asked for.

238
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:17,090
To recap: distribute a
negative to every term,

239
00:12:17,110 --> 00:12:21,825
factor completely, multiply
exponents for a power of a power,

240
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:24,895
never split a power or
root over a plus sign,

241
00:12:25,038 --> 00:12:27,930
cancel factors only,
and check with a number.

242
00:12:27,950 --> 00:12:32,073
For practice, filter the College Board's
free Question Bank for equivalent

243
00:12:32,093 --> 00:12:33,128
expressions.

244
00:12:33,211 --> 00:12:36,441
Every question in this video
was written for this video,

245
00:12:36,461 --> 00:12:38,925
in the style of the real test.

246
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:43,405
Next up: SAT nonlinear
functions and graphs.

247
00:12:43,425 --> 00:12:45,747
If this helped, subscribe so you catch it.
